  "term": "ideogram",
  "definition": "An ideogram is a written sign that conveys meaning through its own form rather than through the spoken name of what it represents, often as a picture-like symbol. In historical accounts of writing, it refers to an early stage of script development and is contrasted with phonographic writing, which represents words or sounds.",
